+# DLSS Neural Rendering
+
+This patch adds NVIDIA NGX feature 18 (DLSS Neural Rendering) to the
+Vulkan RTX Remix renderer.
+
+## Current mode
+
+- Runs after DLSS Super Resolution or DLSS Ray Reconstruction.
+- Uses the full-resolution linear HDR result as the NR color input.
+- Uses Remix depth and motion vectors as temporal guides.
+- Writes to a separate FP16 texture, then copies back only after a successful
+  NGX evaluation.
+- Preserves the original DLSS/RR result when feature creation or evaluation
+  fails.
+- Latches off after three consecutive evaluation failures.
+- Supports live tuning from the Remix menu without restarting the game.
+
+Feature 18 runs at a scaling ratio of 1.0 in this integration.
+It does not perform a second upscale.
+
+## Runtime
+
+Place NVIDIA's signed `nvngx_dlssnr.dll` next to the 64-bit Remix renderer in
+`.trex`. The API integration targets runtime version 310.8.0.0.
+
+## Options
+
+Options are stored under `rtx.neuralRendering`:
+
+- `enableNeuralRendering`
+- `neuralRenderingPreset`
+- `neuralRenderingStyle`
+- `neuralRenderingIntensity`
+- `neuralRenderingLocalToneStrength`
+- `neuralRenderingLocalStructureStrength`
+- `neuralRenderingSkinStructureStrength`
+- `neuralRenderingAutoMask`
+- `neuralRenderingUICorrection`
+- `neuralRenderingDepthMode`
+- `neuralRenderingMotionScaleX`
+- `neuralRenderingMotionScaleY`
+
+## Diagnostics
+
+Search the Remix renderer log for:
+
+- `Created DLSS Neural Rendering feature 18`
+- `DLSS Neural Rendering produced its first frame`
+- `DLSS Neural Rendering evaluation failed`
+
+The in-game Remix menu also reports successful and failed evaluation counts.
